{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared sentinel inputs for the unit-level TS <-> Kotlin parity sweep.",
    "Both runners read this file and emit a flat map of named scalars, compared by",
    "compare-units.py. Deliberately weighted towards inputs a real GPX trace never",
    "produces -- poles, antimeridian, zero-length segments, colinear points -- because",
    "the end-to-end cascade already covers the ordinary path well.",
    "Coordinates are in DEGREES with elevation in metres (the :elevation public API)."
  ],

